<title>SPAIN: Spain's Sept trade deficit shrinks 8.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain's Sept trade deficit shrinks 8.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The customs department of the Economy Ministry gave the following figures (billions of pesetas):</p>
<p> TRADE BALANCE		SEPT 96	 AUG 96     SEPT 95</p>
<p> Exports		     1,040.7	  754.2	 995.4</p>
<p> Imports		     1,341.8	  934.2     1,282.6</p>
<p> Deficit/surplus	    -301.0	 -179.9	-287.2</p>
<p> Def/surplus yr to date -2,037.1     -1,736.1    -2,234.3</p>
<p>NOTE - The figures are customs-cleared data.  </p>
<p> TRADE BALANCE (EU)	SEPT 96	 AUG 96	SEPT 95</p>
<p> Exports		     757.2	   501.1	  754.7</p>
<p> Imports		     914.0	   566.3	  865.7</p>
<p> Deficit/surplus	  -156.7	   -65.2	 -111.0</p>
<p> Def/surplus yr to date -736.5	  -579.8	 -827.3</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
